  <h2>Accessibility &amp; SEO Considerations</h2>
  <p>Before you small-text everything, two important caveats:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Screen readers:</strong> Unicode small text characters may not be interpreted as the letters they visually resemble. If your bio contains critical information (like a website URL or contact method), keep it in regular text so screen readers can parse it correctly</li>
    <li><strong>Search engines:</strong> Google and other search engines treat Unicode characters as different from standard letters. "ʰᵉˡˡᵒ" is not the same as "hello" to a search crawler. Don't put keywords you want to rank for in small text format</li>
  </ol>

